  "description": "<p>When creating Binary resources then reindexing, I observed that the count of NonRdfSourceDescription and all resources at the fcr:stats endpoint was changing after a subsequent reindexing. After more testing, it appears that when adding binaries the NonRdfSourceDescription entry is generally not being added, although I did observe that when I run a bulk object creation script that the NonRdfSourceDescription count goes up about half as much as the Binary count.</p>\n\n<p>To verify this issue, run <tt>mvn jetty:run -pl fcrepo-webapp</tt> on main, go to:<br/>\n<a href=\"http://localhost:8088/rest/fcr:stats\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/fcr:stats</a></p>\n\n<p>You should see all zeros (assuming you were starting fresh). Then create a couple binaries in the UI, and visit fcr:stats again. You should now see the <tt><a href=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#Binary\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#Binary</a></tt> count equal to the number of binaries you created, but there are no <tt>NonRdfSourceDescription</tt> entries.</p>\n\n<p>Next, stop jetty, and then run it with reindexing turned on:</p>\n\n<p><tt>mvn -Dfcrepo.rebuild=true -rf fcrepo-webapp jetty:run</tt></p>\n\n<p>Now go to fcr:stats again, and there will be a <tt>NonRdfSourceDescription</tt> count equal to the number of binaries. The <tt>resource_count</tt> also will have gone up, since it includes the <tt>NonRdfSourceDescriptions</tt></p>",
